+## D06 current composed policy consumption
+
+The current final proof's separately approved Core ResourcePolicy/2 also owns
+composed validation limits. The existing historical path retains its 30-second
+read ceiling and Context2048/Focus512 identities. The current path requires
+Context8192/Focus512 identities across the entire three-model fixture and uses
+the approved120-second ceiling on both development-native-goal calls and
+original composed start/await calls, including first-forward warm observations,
+source reads, noninterference and independent-stage comparisons. It does not
+refresh a submitted deadline, change any read clock or grant extra model time.
+
+Current dual-stage Answer evidence must bind the exact Rust-decoded original
+AnswerArgs budget to the separately pinned original budget:8192 shared input
+tokens and120000ms. Historical2048/30 arguments or a changed source-budget
+projection cannot satisfy current qualification. Existing actual event/charge,
+complete source, native input, resource/OS telemetry, drain and held-out proof
+requirements remain in force. Controller acceptance, synthetic sources and a
+configured resource ceiling cannot replace any of those gates. Primitive p95
+measurements remain distinct from actual composed/end-to-end observations.
+
+This is a private evidence-validator decision under existing D06, with no new
+wire fields or digest inputs. Native historical receipts stay unchanged; current
+limits flow only from the exact policy already approved by the final decision.
